  "description": "Given two strings `text1` and `text2`, return the length of their **longest common subsequence**. If there is no common subsequence, return `0`.\n\nA **subsequence** of a string is a new string generated from the original string with some characters (can be none) deleted without changing the relative order of the remaining characters.\n\n- For example, `\"ace\"` is a subsequence of `\"abcde\"`.\n\nA **common subsequence** of two strings is a subsequence that is common to both strings.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "text1 = \"abcde\", text2 = \"ace\"",
      "output": "3",
      "explanation": "The longest common subsequence is \"ace\" and its length is 3."
    },
    {
      "input": "text1 = \"abc\", text2 = \"abc\"",
      "output": "3",
      "explanation": "The longest common subsequence is \"abc\" and its length is 3."
    },
    {
      "input": "text1 = \"abc\", text2 = \"def\"",
      "output": "0",
      "explanation": "There is no such common subsequence, so the result is 0."
    },
    {
      "input": "text1 = \"abc\", text2 = \"ac\"",
      "output": "2",
      "explanation": "The longest common subsequence is \"ac\" with length 2 (matches the step-by-step dry-run visualization)."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= text1.length, text2.length <= 1000",
    "text1 and text2 consist of only lowercase English characters."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Use a 2D dynamic programming grid where dp[i][j] stores the length of the LCS for text1[0..i-1] and text2[0..j-1].",
    "If text1[i-1] matches text2[j-1], take the diagonal value plus one: dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1.",
    "If characters do not match, take the maximum of the top cell and left cell: dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])."
  ],
  "externalLinks": [
    {
      "platform": "leetcode",
      "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-common-subsequence/"
    }
  ],
  "starterCode": {
    "javascript": "/**\n * @param {string} text1\n * @param {string} text2\n * @return {number}\n */\nfunction longestCommonSubsequence(text1, text2) {\n    // Your code here\n}"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "language": "javascript",
      "timeComplexity": "O(M * N)",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(M * N)",
      "explanation": "2D tabular dynamic programming. Build an (M+1) x (N+1) grid. If characters match, take dp[i-1][j-1] + 1. Otherwise, take max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]).",
      "code": "function longestCommonSubsequence(text1, text2) {\n    const m = text1.length;\n    const n = text2.length;\n    const dp = Array.from({ length: m + 1 }, () => new Array(n + 1).fill(0));\n\n    for (let i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n        for (let j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n            if (text1[i - 1] === text2[j - 1]) {\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;\n            } else {\n                dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    return dp[m][n];\n}"
    }
  ],
